["er.eventlog.import-anchor/1",{"authority":{"logical_scope":"entity-runtime","stream_identity":"01a0cab7-1ed7-77a5-8384-ff10c92e7ad6","tenant":"planning"},"completeness":"available_evidence_only","evidence":[],"instance":{"entity":"aep.entity","fields":{"document":{"events":[],"fields":{"$aep":{"archived":false,"metadata":{"created_at":0,"id":"MIGcd8bb963a673d1d9de55941b55cf8593bf1196b243cadf701724213f19b9ad5c","locator":"ep://planning/store/story/event-envelope","provenance":{"created_by":"system","updated_by":"system"},"revision":7,"type":"aep.story/v1","updated_at":0}},"body":"# Story: A reference event envelope type\n\n## Outcome\n\nShells agree on the shape around a `DomainEvent` — `event_id`, `recorded_at`, `correlation`,\n`causation`, `actor` — without the kernel touching a clock or an id generator.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nAn `Envelope<DomainEvent>` type in a crate outside `entity-core` (the SPI crate, or its own), with\nthe four-field argument `domain_event.rs` in `engineering-protocols` makes for correlation ≠\ncausation; `entity execute` gains flags to supply the envelope values and prints enveloped events\nwhen they are given; R-72 stays as stated — the kernel's event carries none of this.\n","relations":[{"derived_from":"epic:kernel"},{"decomposes":"epic:the-shell"},{"depends_on":"story:provider-spi"}],"status":"implemented","summary":"event_id, recorded_at, correlation, causation and actor around a DomainEvent — defined outside entity-core, so shells agree on the shape without the kernel touching a clock.","title":"A reference event envelope type"},"lifecycle_state":"implemented"}},"id":"MIGcd8bb963a673d1d9de55941b55cf8593bf1196b243cadf701724213f19b9ad5c","lifecycle_state":"recorded","revision":7,"version":1},"order":"per_kind_only","subject":["aep.entity","MIGcd8bb963a673d1d9de55941b55cf8593bf1196b243cadf701724213f19b9ad5c"]}]